This package provides the kim_init, kim_query, kim_interactions, and
the pair_style kim command which are wrappers on the Knowledgebase of
Interatomic Models (KIM) repository of interatomic potentials, so that
they can be used by LAMMPS scripts.

Information about the KIM project can be found at https://openkim.org.
The KIM project is lead by Ellad B. Tadmor and Ryan S. Elliott (UMN).
Ryan Elliott is the main developer for the KIM API and he also
maintains the code that implements these commands.

Using this package requires the KIM-API library and its models
(interatomic potentials) to be downloaded and installed on your system.
The library can be automatically downloaded and built during the
compilation of LAMMPS or installed separately on your system, which must
be done before building LAMMPS with this package.  Outside of testing
LAMMPS, it is generally recommended to perform a separate installation of
the KIM-API so that its tools are available directly.  Details of the
download, build, and install process for the KIM-API are given in the
KIM-API documentation.  Also see the LAMMPS manual for general
information on building LAMMPS with packages requiring external
libraries. Once you have successfully built LAMMPS with this package,
you can test it using one of the input files in the examples dir:

./build/lmp -in lammps/examples/kim/in.kim-ex.melt

These commands were written by Ryan S. Elliott (UMN), Ellad B. Tadmor (UMN),
Yaser Afshar (UMN), Ilia Nikiforov (UMN), and Axel Kohlmeyer (Temple U).
